h-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/system-search-parameters#4-full-date--timezone-offset-precision","content":"Varying Precision: Searches using year (`ge2026`) or month (`2026-09`) automatically expand to exact start and end millisecond ranges, preventing false negatives.","locale":"en"},"122":{"id":"/docs/v3/system-search-parameters-18","page_id":"/docs/v3/system-search-parameters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/system-search-parameters#4-full-date--timezone-offset-precision","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"123":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","type":"page","content":"Temporal & Dual-Database Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v3 (Preview)"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","locale":"en"},"124":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","content":"Architecture breakdown of Burni v3 active resource and temporal history segregation","locale":"en"},"125":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#temporal--dual-database-architecture","content":"Temporal & Dual-Database Architecture","locale":"en"},"126":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#architectural-topology","content":"Architectural Topology","locale":"en"},"127":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#1-separation-of-concerns","content":"1\\. Separation of Concerns","locale":"en"},"128":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#2-provenance--audit-guarantees","content":"2\\. Provenance & Audit Guarantees","locale":"en"},"129":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#operational-advantages","content":"Operational Advantages","locale":"en"},"130":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#temporal--dual-database-architecture","content":"Enterprise health systems demand auditability: every resource change or deletion creates an immutable record. Over time, historical versions dwarf active resources, leading to index bloat and degraded read latency.","locale":"en"},"131":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#temporal--dual-database-architecture","content":"**Burni v3** introduces a **Temporal & Dual-Database Architecture** to solve this problem cleanly.","locale":"en"},"132":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#1-separation-of-concerns","content":"**Primary Database**:","locale":"en"},"133":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#1-separation-of-concerns","content":"Contains strictly the current active resources.","locale":"en"},"134":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#1-separation-of-concerns","content":"Keeps working sets in memory for maximum throughput on clinical lookups and complex search queries.","locale":"en"},"135":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#1-separation-of-concerns","content":"**Temporal Database**:","locale":"en"},"136":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#1-separation-of-concerns","content":"Stores historical revisions (`*_history` collections), HTTP request contexts, and audit provenance data.","locale":"en"},"137":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#1-separation-of-concerns","content":"Indexed on timestamps, versions (`versionId`), and resource identifiers.","locale":"en"},"138":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#2-provenance--audit-guarantees","content":"**BundleRequest Capture**: Every version records its originating HTTP headers, transaction boundaries, and actor credentials.","locale":"en"},"139":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#2-provenance--audit-guarantees","content":"**High-Precision vread**: Historical requests (`[baseUrl]/[type]/[id]/_history/[vid]`) route straight to the temporal store without impacting active resource queries.","locale":"en"},"140":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#operational-advantages","content":"**Tiered Storage Optimization**:","locale":"en"},"141":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#operational-advantages","content":"Keep Primary DB on high-performance NVMe volumes, while placing Temporal DB on cost-effective storage tiers.","locale":"en"},"142":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#operational-advantages","content":"**Independent Backup & Recovery**:","locale":"en"},"143":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#operational-advantages","content":"Establish dedicated snapshot policies for operational data versus long-term audit archives.","locale":"en"},"144":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#operational-advantages","content":"**Transparent Execution**:","locale":"en"},"145":{"id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v3/temporal-architecture#operational-advantages","content":"Burni's internal Data Operator layer abstracts database routing completely—no custom code is required at the API route level.","locale":"en"},"146":{"id":"/docs/v2","page_id":"/docs/v2","type":"page","content":"Burni v2 (LTS) Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2","locale":"en"},"147":{"id":"/docs/v2-0","page_id":"/docs/v2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2","content":"Documentation and guide for Burni v2 LTS (v2.8) release","locale":"en"},"148":{"id":"/docs/v2-1","page_id":"/docs/v2","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2#burni-v2-lts-documentation-guide","content":"Burni v2 (LTS) Documentation Guide","locale":"en"},"149":{"id":"/docs/v2-2","page_id":"/docs/v2","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2#core-sections","content":"Core Sections","locale":"en"},"150":{"id":"/docs/v2-3","page_id":"/docs/v2","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2#exploring-next-generation-features","content":"Exploring Next Generation Features","locale":"en"},"151":{"id":"/docs/v2-4","page_id":"/docs/v2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2#burni-v2-lts-documentation-guide","content":"Welcome to the &#x2A;*Burni v