d-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"The code about search parameters can be found in `models\\FHIR\\queryBuild.js` and `models\\FHIR\\searchParameterQueryHandler.js` files.","locale":"en"},"288":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-5","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"`queryBuild.js`: get single MongoDB query object from data type.","locale":"en"},"289":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-6","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"`searchParameterQueryHandler.js`: using `queryBuild.js` and get fully MongoDB query object from HTTP query param.","locale":"en"},"290":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-7","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"Some search parameters from generator will got missing or incorrect. You can fix by using methods in `models\\FHIR\\searchParameterQueryHandler.js`.","locale":"en"},"291":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-8","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"FHIR R4 defines `Bundle.composition` and `Bundle.message` as reference search parameters. Burni resolves them from the SearchParameter Registry and evaluates only `entry[0].resource`:","locale":"en"},"292":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-9","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"`composition` — `document` Bundles whose first entry is a `Composition`","locale":"en"},"293":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-10","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"`message` — `message` Bundles whose first entry is a `MessageHeader`","locale":"en"},"294":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-11","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"Burni does not fan out across all `entry` elements. Only the first embedded resource participates in these special searches.","locale":"en"},"295":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-12","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#direct-identity-search","content":"Supported value forms include relative `ResourceType/id`, a bare id normalized to the fixed target type, and an absolute URL that matches `entry[0].fullUrl`. Versioned, contained, and logical identifier references are rejected.","locale":"en"},"296":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-13","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#direct-identity-search","content":"Example URLs:","locale":"en"},"297":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-14","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#chained-search","content":"After the inline hop, Burni applies the target resource SearchParameter plan from the Registry. Examples:","locale":"en"},"298":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-15","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#chained-search","content":"`composition.patient` follows `Composition::patient` and may fan out to `Patient` and `Group`. `MessageHeader.focus` is an open reference target, so a type filter is required before chaining further:","locale":"en"},"299":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-16","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#chained-search","content":"This request is rejected with HTTP 400 and `missing-type-filter`.","locale":"en"},"300":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-17","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#limitations","content":"Only `entry[0].resource` is evaluated; later entries do not affect results even when they contain a matching Composition or MessageHeader.","locale":"en"},"301":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-18","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#limitations","content":"Bundle type and first-entry resource type must match; invalid stored Bundles simply do not match rather than returning parameter errors.","locale":"en"},"302":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Search Parameters"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","locale":"en"},"303":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameters-overview","content":"Search parameters overview","locale":"en"},"304":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameter-types","content":"Search Parameter Types","locale":"en"},"305":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#parameters-for-all-resources","content":"Parameters for all resources","locale":"en"},"306":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-result-parameters","content":"Search result parameters","locale":"en"},"307":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#derived-indexes-and-custom-searchparameters","content":"Derived indexes and custom SearchParameters","locale":"en"},"308":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"Non-temporal derived index boundary","locale":"en"},"309":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameters-overview","content":"The burni currently support FHIR search operations below:","locale":"en"},"310":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameter-types","content":"Number","locale":"en"},"311":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameter-types","content":"Date/DateTime","locale":"en"},"312":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameter-types","content":"String","locale":"en"},"313":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameter-types","content":"Token","locale":"en"},"314":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameter-types","content":"Reference","locale":"en"},"315":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#parameters-for-all-resources","content":"\\_id","locale":"en"},"316":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#parameters-for-all-resources","content":"\\_lastUpdated","locale":"en"},"317":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-result-parameters","content":"\\_count","locale":"en"},"318":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#derived-indexes-and-custom-searchparameters","content":"The SearchParameter Registry owns query correctness; MongoDB derived indexes only improve query performance. They are separate lifecycle concerns.","locale":"en"},"319":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-16","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#derived-indexes-and-custom-searchparameters","content":"First-phase provisioning creates derived indexes for **approved built-in temporal and non-temporal SearchParameters**. Each included lookup must be active, compilable, pass the corresponding index policy, and expose a safe index contract for its extraction/projection branch.","locale":"en"},"320":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-17","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"**token**: system-code or system-value correlation for Coding/CodeableConcept/Identifier/ContactPoint; `:text` queries are not indexed.","locale":"en"},"321":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-18","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"**reference**: indexes stored `reference` only; `Reference.type` target guards remain runtime filters.","locale":"en"},"322":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"**string**: equality indexes on exact projected leaves only; default prefix and `:contains` keep regex semantics without B-tree claims.","locale":"en"},"323":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"**number / quantity**: use existing numeric BSON fields; `sa`, `eb`, and `ap` comparators are not supported in the capability matrix.","locale":"en"},"324":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"**uri**: raw URI single-field index shared by exact, `:above`, and `:below`.","locale":"en"},"325":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-22","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"**array correlation**: only a single verifiable array scope is admitted; parallel multikey, positional paths, and unsafe branches produce stable rejection diagnostics.","locale":"en"},"326":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-23","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"**Custom database SearchParameters** remain executable by default but are **not** added to the desired index manifest, so they do not receive derived indexes. That does not disable the query; it means MongoDB may use COLLSCAN. When performance indexes are missing, run `npm run mongodb:verify` to inspect drift and run `npm run mongodb:provision` as part of deployment.","locale":"en"},"327":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-24","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#non-temporal-derived-index-boundary","content":"The expected derived index state is merged into the runtime-generated desired index manifest. See the MongoDB provisioning section in Deploy.","locale":"en"},"328":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","type":"page","content":"Configuration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","locale":"en"},"329":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#configconfigjs","content":"config\\config.js","locale":"en"},"330":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#dotenv","content":"dotenv","locale":"en"},"331":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#generate-code","content":"Generate code","locale":"en"},"332":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-3","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#configconfigjs","content":"This file is config what resources you want to support.","locale":"en"},"333":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-4","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#configconfigjs","content":"If you want to support all resources, you can run command below:","locale":"en"},"334":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-5","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#configconfigjs","content":"This will generate config.js for all resources.","locale":"en"},"335":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-6","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#dotenv","content":"`.env` in root path.","locale":"en"},"336":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-7","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#generate-code","content":"After configuration above, you need to run script below to generate js code of API and mongoose model.","locale":"en"},"337":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration-8","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/configuration#generate-code","content":"`TypeError: genParamFunc[type] is not a function` is meaning that method of search parameter not support now.","locale":"en"},"338":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"page","content":"Deploy","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","locale":"en"},"339":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#with-nodejs","content":"With Node.JS","locale":"en"},"340":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#with-docker-compose","content":"With docker-compose","locale":"en"},"341":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#docker-compose-deploy","content":"docker-compose deploy","locale":"en"},"342":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-3","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#mongodb-schema-and-index-provisioning","content":"MongoDB schema and index provisioning","locale":"en"},"343":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-4","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#pre-deployment-provisioning-recommended","content":"Pre-deployment provisioning (recommended)","locale":"en"},"344":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-5","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"Read-only verify","locale":"en"},"345":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-6","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#id-duplicate-audit-read-only","content":"`id` duplicate audit (read-only)","locale":"en"},"346":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-7","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#startup-opt-in","content":"Startup opt-in","locale":"en"},"347":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-8","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#relationship-to-searchparameter-derived-indexes","content":"Relationship to SearchParameter derived indexes","locale":"en"},"348":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-9","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#with-nodejs","content":"You will see console printing the information below:","locale":"en"},"349":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-10","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#with-docker-compose","content":"The example of `docker-compose.yaml` file in root path","locale":"en"},"350":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-11","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#mongodb-schema-and-index-provisioning","content":"Burni sets Mongoose `autoCreate` and `autoIndex` to `false` by default. Model registration only means models are registered inside the application process; it does **not** guarantee that MongoDB collections or indexes exist. Production deployments should run provisioning before application startup, or explicitly enable startup opt-in.","locale":"en"},"351":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-12","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#mongodb-schema-and-index-provisioning","content":"The desired collection and index manifest is generated deterministically at runtime from registered models, the model catalog, approved built-in temporal definitions, and non-temporal SearchParameter derived indexes that pass policy. The manifest stores `artifactIdentity` (compiled SearchParameter artifact) and `derivedIndexPolicy.searchParameterPolicyVersion` (non-temporal index policy). Provisioning reconciles MongoDB against that generated manifest, persists results in `MongoProvisioningState`, and uses `MongoProvisioningLock` with a database-scoped lease for multi-instance runs. Use `writeDesiredManifestArtifact()` when you need a persisted JSON copy (default path `models/mongodb/provisioning/artifacts/desired-index-manifest.json`).","locale":"en"},"352":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-13","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#pre-deployment-provisioning-recommended","content":"Configure the same MongoDB connection environment variables as the application (`MONGODB_CONNECTION_URL`, or `MONGODB_HOSTS` / `MONGODB_PORTS` / `MONGODB_NAME`), then run:","locale":"en"},"353":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-14","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#pre-deployment-provisioning-recommended","content":"This command runs control-plane initialization, acquires the lock, creates collections, creates baseline indexes, creates approved built-in derived indexes (temporal and non-temporal SearchParameters), runs verify, and persists the manifest checksum and drift summary. Exit code `0` on success; any failed phase returns a non-zero status.","locale":"en"},"354":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-15","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#pre-deployment-provisioning-recommended","content":"**Partial completion and retry**: Provisioning is additive-only and does not roll back collections or indexes that were already created. If a run fails midway, completed DDL remains in place; rerunning `mongodb:provision` continues from the desired/actual diff. After lock lease expiry, another process can reclaim the expired lock and retry.","locale":"en"},"355":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-16","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"`mongodb:verify` performs **no DDL** and does not modify data. It reads actual collections and indexes and reports:","locale":"en"},"356":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-17","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**missing**: indexes expected by the manifest but absent in the database","locale":"en"},"357":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-18","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**extra**: indexes present in the database but not declared in the manifest (reported only, never deleted)","locale":"en"},"358":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-19","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**mismatch**: indexes whose key or options do not match the expected identity","locale":"en"},"359":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-20","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**manifest identity drift**: the current desired manifest checksum or version differs from the value stored in `MongoProvisioningState` for the latest successful run","locale":"en"},"360":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-21","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"Verify failure uses exit code `2`.","locale":"en"},"361":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-22","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#id-duplicate-audit-read-only","content":"Scans resource and history collections for duplicate `id` values for a future unique-migration clean-audit gate. It **does not modify data**. General provisioning does **not** automatically change an existing `id` index to unique.","locale":"en"},"362":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-23","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#startup-opt-in","content":"By default, `node server.js` does **not** run provisioning. Application readiness (`mongodb.ready`) and provisioning readiness are separate. Missing performance indexes (including non-temporal derived indexes) do not block HTTP listen, but queries may fall back to COLLSCAN; `mongodb:verify` diagnostics report missing performance indexes.","locale":"en"},"363":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-24","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#startup-opt-in","content":"To wait for a full provisioning run before application ready, set:","locale":"en"},"364":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-25","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#startup-opt-in","content":"or `MONGODB_PROVISION_ON_STARTUP=1`. When enabled, server bootstrap runs the same locked run as `mongodb:provision` before listen. On failure it does not declare ready, does not listen, and exits with a non-zero status. Production deployments should still prefer the standalone deployment command over startup opt-in.","locale":"en"},"365":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-26","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#relationship-to-searchparameter-derived-indexes","content":"The derived index manifest merges temporal and policy-approved non-temporal built-in lookups (token, reference, string, number, quantity, uri). Custom database SearchParameters remain executable but do not create derived indexes by default. Derived index reconcile is additive-only: missing indexes can be created by `provision`, while extra or mismatched indexes are reported by `verify` and never auto-deleted; query runtime does not use `$hint`. Rollback can disable the new policy or restore a manifest version without auto-deleting indexes already created. See Search parameters overview and ADR 0010.","locale":"en"},"366":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","locale":"en"},"367":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"With git","locale":"en"},"368":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"Please confirm that you have the:","locale":"en"},"369":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"git","locale":"en"},"370":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-3","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"Node.js >= 22","locale":"en"},"371":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-4","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"MongoDB > 4.2","locale":"en"},"372":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-5","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"Clone from git","locale":"en"},"373":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-6","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"Install dependencies","locale":"en"},"374":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-7","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"after installation, let's starting configuration","locale":"en"},"375":{"id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler","page_id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler","type":"page","content":"searchParameterQueryHandler","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Code API Documentation","Models","Code API Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler","locale":"en"},"376":{"id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler#functions","content":"Functions","locale":"en"},"377":{"id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler#getstringqueryquery-paramssearchfields-queryfieldname","content":"getStringQuery(query, paramsSearchFields, queryFieldName)","locale":"en"},"378":{"id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/code-api-documentation/models/fhir/search-parameter-query-handler#getaddressqueryquery-queryfieldname","content":"getAddressQuery(query, queryFieldName)","locale":"en"},"379":{"id":"/docs/v2/code